# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# Compiled output
/dist
/tmp
/out-tsc
# Compodoc's input table for the nxs- Storybook, written before every Storybook run.
/libs/shared/satori-components/documentation.json
/bazel-out
**/target/

# Node
/node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# IDEs and editors
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/mcp.json
.history/*

# Cursor debug logs
.cursor/debug*.log

# Miscellaneous
/.angular/cache
.sass-cache/
/connect.lock
/coverage
/libpeerconnection.log
testem.log
/typings
__screenshots__/

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.nx/cache
.nx/workspace-data
.angular

vitest.config.*.timestamp*

# Playwright output from local evidence runs
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Environment files. `.env` alone matched one exact path, which let
# `.env.arender` be committed with a credential in it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example

# Nuxeo server configuration (secrets, bind-mounted into the container)
/nuxeo-conf/*.conf
!/nuxeo-conf/*.sample.conf
# Customer-facing docs copied into the platform package at build time by
# scripts/sync-platform-docs.mjs. docs/ is the single source; these are generated.
/libs/platform/extension-reference.md

# Nx generators compiled into the platform package at build time by
# scripts/build-platform-generators.mjs. tools/satori-generators/ is the single source.
/libs/platform/generators/
/libs/platform/generators.json

# Staging dir for the publishability gate's declaration typecheck. Always removed in a
# finally block; ignored so an interrupted run cannot be committed.
/.tmp-publishability/

# Staging dir for the upgrade rehearsal. Always removed in a finally block; ignored so
# an interrupted run cannot be committed.
/.tmp-upgrade-rehearsal/

# Playwright E2E output: JSON results, traces, videos and failure screenshots.
/dist/e2e/

# Rendered documentation diagrams. Regenerated by scripts/render-mermaid.mjs from the
# Mermaid in documentation/, which is the source of truth.
/dist/documentation-diagrams/

# Demo-deck screenshots. Regenerated by scripts/demo-deck/capture.mjs against a running
# instance, and roughly 4 MB per capture. docs/demo-deck-plan.md already told readers this
# directory was ignored; until now it was not, so every capture left the working tree dirty
# and a `git add -A` would have committed the images. The deck JSON and the capture script
# are the sources of truth and stay tracked.
/tools/video/shots/

# Local agent tool configuration. Machine-specific, and it carries per-developer
# permission grants that should not be imposed on anyone else's checkout.
/.claude/settings.json
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Nested git worktrees created by the agent tooling. These are full checkouts of this
# repository living inside it, so every project they contain is a SECOND definition of a
# project Nx already knows — and Nx refuses the whole graph rather than guessing:
#
#   NX  Failed to process project graph.
#   The following projects are defined in multiple locations: nuxeo-satori-template, browse, …
#
# That takes out lint, test, build, typecheck and api-surface together, locally only, in a way
# that reads like a broken branch. `nx reset` does not help, because the duplication is real
# rather than cached. Ignored here rather than in `.nxignore` because Nx reads this file too and
# a nested checkout must never be committable in the first place.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Ad-hoc debugging scratch files. Kept out of the tree rather than deleted, because
# they are useful locally while the Nuxeo tree API and drawer are being worked on —
# but they are not part of the product and two of them bypass the app entirely
# (raw fetch against Nuxeo, no auth interceptor), so they must never ship.
/test-tree-api.html
/apps/nuxeo-ui/src/diagnostic.html
/apps/nuxeo-ui-e2e/screenshot-debug.spec.ts

# SonarCloud analysis artifacts (generated during local scans)
.scannerwork/
.sonar/

# Per-ticket dev-server proxy configs and Nuxeo conf, generated by
# .cursor/skills/fix-bug/scripts/new-ticket-workspace.sh. The tracked proxy.conf.json points
# at the shared instance on :8080; a ticket workspace runs its own container on its own port
# and needs its own config. Machine- and run-specific, and the conf directory is a copy of
# nuxeo-conf/ which carries credentials — neither may ever be committed.
/apps/nuxeo-ui/proxy.conf.ticket-*.json
/.nuxeo-conf/
/env.sh

# Local security planning notes, kept for agent reference rather than shipped. Deliberately
# untracked: the file is a dated prose snapshot of mutable state — open alert counts, Sonar
# issue counts, per-file `.subscribe()` tallies — which is the failure mode CLAUDE.md records
# for summaries that go stale silently and are believed anyway. Ignored rather than merely
# untracked so a stray `git add -A` cannot put it back.
/docs/security-next-steps.md
apps/nuxeo-ui/public/agentic-ui-config/bootstrap.json
apps/nuxeo-ui/public/agentic-ui-config/manifest.json
apps/nuxeo-ui/public/agentic-ui-config/layouts.json
apps/nuxeo-ui/public/agentic-ui-config/layouts/
apps/nuxeo-ui/public/i18n/zz.json

# Local planning scratch. Two stray files were swept into a translation PR by `git add -A`, and
# both had to be caught by a reviewer: a plan under `.cursor/plans/` and a 368-line prompt saved as
# `scripts/Untitled`. Ignoring the first did not generalise, so extensionless scratch under
# `scripts/` is ignored too — everything real in that directory has an extension.
.cursor/plans/
scripts/Untitled*

# a11y-scout's per-scan output, which lands at the repository root and cannot be moved: its
# ScanPageOptions has no outDir, only generateReport() does. So 11y/.gitignore covers
# the consolidated reports but never these, and a 12-minute 11y:scan -- modes leaves a dozen
# untracked directories here that a git add -A would commit.
/a11y-reports/